%%label I. Très modéré
%%note D flat major. Murmuring violas and harp; a call for cor anglais and horn; a floating theme for the flute; a middle section that bends the call into the whole-tone scale and rises to four descending major chords; the theme returns with the call beneath it, and the call closes the movement.
X:1
T:Debussy’s Missing Symphony
T:I. Très modéré
C:Lor, in the manner of Debussy
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:"Très modéré" 3/8=46
%%score [fl ob eh cl bn] [hn tp] tm {hu hl} [v1 v2 va vc cb]
% The score is written at sounding pitch. Dynamics in the wind, brass and double-bass parts are set one to three levels below the strings to balance the playback samples of this site; they are a playback compromise, not dynamics for live players.
